# Non-secret development-container defaults.
#
# Set LABBY_ENV_FILE to a private host file when runtime secrets or endpoint
# overrides are required. Never put credentials in this tracked example.

# Shared Assistant / Agent OpenAI-compatible provider. Agent execution requires
# this base URL; the API key is optional when the endpoint does not require auth.
# ExGPT deployments also expose the /v1/sessions lifecycle extensions used by
# Labby for create, cancel, and close. The URL must be reachable from the Labby
# runtime itself: 127.0.0.1 is valid only when the provider is co-located in the
# same host/container. Embedded URL credentials are rejected; use the API-key
# variable for bearer authentication instead.
# LABBY_PHOENIX_OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:43871/v1
# LABBY_PHOENIX_OPENAI_API_KEY=
